**Designing isolated native browser tests**
**Optimizing test isolation and cache control**

I’m considering ways to avoid navigation side effects by resetting upstream state or warming cache with fresh contexts before each test. I want to keep tests standalone using existing verify methods without modifying old tests and explore using CDP-driven navigation with fresh browser contexts or manual cache restoration. I’m weighing native versus mock tests for speed and looking into controlled startup of the registry suite on fixed versions.
